    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1366" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδι-έξοδος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that cannot be gone
			through</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἄπειρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					204a14
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>having no outlet</i>, of places, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Mith.</u>
				100
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.957d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>unable to get out,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				11.395
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Nicarch.
			</span></i>), cf <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.679b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ocell.
				1.15
			</span></i>.</div>
